#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082985 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dccdc3ad-6acb-57ae-83ef-95ffedfbff2f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Velocity Vector of a Particle Moving in Two Dimensions"}] :question/id #uuid "9b28994b-b161-504b-8993-d300f464a2cc" :question/math-academy-id "e-616" :question/problem "The position vector $\\mathbf{r}$ of a particle $P$ relative to a fixed origin $O$ at time $t > 0$ is given by\n$\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 3t^3, 2t^2\\rangle$.\nCalculate the velocity vector $\\mathbf{v}$." :question/worked-solution "The particle's velocity vector is given by the derivative of its position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nv &= \\frac{dr}{dt} \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{dx}{dt}, \\frac{dy}{dt}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{d}{dt}(3t^{3}), \\frac{d}{dt}(2t^{2})⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨9t^{2}, 4t⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082986 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ca363e2-c7b7-5196-bd38-10bcc30123ce" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Velocity Vector of a Particle Moving in Two Dimensions at a Given Time"}] :question/id #uuid "768aa1ca-15ff-5307-8184-6dd207f7e061" :question/math-academy-id "e-617" :question/problem "The position vector $\\mathbf{r}$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t > 0$ is given by\n$\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 12t, 2t^3\\rangle$.\nCalculate the velocity vector $\\mathbf{v}$ at time $t=1$." :question/worked-solution "The particle's velocity vector is given by the derivative of its position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nv &= \\frac{dr}{dt} \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{dx}{dt}, \\frac{dy}{dt}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{d}{dt}(12t), \\frac{d}{dt}(2t^{3})⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨12, 6t^{2}⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=1$, we substitute into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nv(1) &= ⟨12, 6(1)^{2}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨12, 6⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082987 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "646467d1-f764-5a3c-b03b-7d74e588611d" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Speed of a Particle at a Given Time"}] :question/id #uuid "b9a41b06-e359-5e55-bad3-37922a87db14" :question/math-academy-id "e-618" :question/problem "The position vector $\\mathbf{r}$ of a particle $P$ relative to a fixed origin $O$ at time $t > 0$ is given by\n$\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 6t^2+2, 2t^3\\rangle$.\nCalculate the speed of the particle at time $t=2$." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the velocity vector $\\mathbf{v}$. Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nv &= \\frac{dr}{dt} \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{dx}{dt}, \\frac{dy}{dt}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{d}{dt}(6t^{2} + 2), \\frac{d}{dt}(2t^{3})⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨12t, 6t^{2}⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=2$, we substitute into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nv(2) &= ⟨12(2), 6(2)^{2}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨24, 24⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed at $t=2$ we calculate the magnitude of $\\mathbf{v}(2)$, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid v(2) \\mid &= \\sqrt{24^{2} + 24^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{2(24^{2})} \\\\\n&= 24\\sqrt{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the speed when $t=2$ is\n\n$$\n24\\sqrt{2}\\approx 33.94\n$$\n\nto two decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082988 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "11a24997-1f1e-5968-a331-980ca14be2f6" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Times at Which a Particle Is Stationary"}] :question/id #uuid "c90c307e-39b7-5159-95bc-9d2961369396" :question/math-academy-id "e-619" :question/problem "A particle $P$ moves in the $x$-$y$ plane (relative to a fixed origin $O$) with position vector\n$[MATH: \\mathbf{r} = \\langle t^2-2t, t^3-3t \\rangle, \\quad t\\in[0,\\infty).]$\n\nCalculate the times at which the particle is stationary." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the velocity vector $\\mathbf{v}$. Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nv &= \\frac{dr}{dt} \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{dx}{dt}, \\frac{dy}{dt}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{d}{dt}(t^{2} - 2t), \\frac{d}{dt}(t^{3} - 3t)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨2t - 2, 3t^{2} - 3⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe particle is stationary when its velocity is zero. This gives,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nv(t) &= 0 \\\\\n⟨2t - 2, 3t^{2} - 3⟩ &= ⟨0, 0⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we need\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2t - 2 &= 0⇒t = 1, \\\\\n3t^{2} - 3 &= 0⇒t = ± 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $t=-1$ is outside of the domain of $t$, so we discard it.\n\nThe solution $t=1$ is the only solution that satisfies both equations, so this is the only time when the object is stationary."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083563 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dccdc3ad-6acb-57ae-83ef-95ffedfbff2f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Velocity Vector of a Particle Moving in Two Dimensions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "928757fc-462c-5ed8-ac32-84141a8c61cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "v = ⟨\\frac{3}{2}t^{3/2} + 8t^{2}, 11t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186080755} {:answer/id #uuid "e9fc8218-c503-50e9-b48f-83bdb8a05bd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "v = ⟨\\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt{t} + 8t, 11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186080756} {:answer/id #uuid "1b0ed92f-f908-5b48-9c39-d4b1303e5ac3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "v = ⟨\\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt{t} + 4t, 10⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186080757} {:answer/id #uuid "4806abdc-248f-555a-b71c-7b47d6b03807" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "v = ⟨\\sqrt{t} + 4t, 11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186080758} {:answer/id #uuid "54905933-f3b0-53e2-b347-53046ba11fca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "v = ⟨\\sqrt{t} + 4t, 11t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186080759}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9fc8218-c503-50e9-b48f-83bdb8a05bd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "v = ⟨\\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt{t} + 8t, 11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186080756} :answer-field/id #uuid "8bc89bd5-53c5-5f27-9693-9655c3e5bb0d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186080754}] :question/id #uuid "57636327-b885-5e06-8c66-a8a3b9fcf6f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-31637" :question/problem "A particle $P$ is moving in the $x$-$y$ plane. Its position vector relative to a fixed origin $O$ is given by\n\n$r = ⟨t^{3/2} + 4t^{2}, 11t - 1⟩, t > 0$.\nCalculate the velocity vector $v$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083681 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "11a24997-1f1e-5968-a331-980ca14be2f6" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Times at Which a Particle Is Stationary"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "92e4bbe9-0831-5fda-822e-472d65ae7fcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081453} {:answer/id #uuid "a619cc01-09ec-5241-b2cc-920974c37d06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The particle is never stationary" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081454} {:answer/id #uuid "a86efacc-fbe1-5c62-b411-915f964880ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t = 0, 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081455} {:answer/id #uuid "b944ece5-fd6a-5f01-b6f2-26886cf02a1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t = 0, 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081456} {:answer/id #uuid "5efa2319-3e5d-5124-93ff-e7a58d3b41f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081457}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92e4bbe9-0831-5fda-822e-472d65ae7fcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081453} :answer-field/id #uuid "326381f8-7d1e-5a68-9df0-524039b7575f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081452}] :question/id #uuid "13836685-e695-5bf2-aaff-9150e2baacb7" :question/math-academy-id "q-51304" :question/problem "A particle $P$ moves in the $x$-$y$ plane (relative to a fixed origin $O$) with position vector\n$[MATH: r = ⟨t^{2}e^{-2t}, (t - 1)^{3}⟩, t ∈ [0, ∞).]$\n\nCalculate the times at which the particle is stationary."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083833 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "646467d1-f764-5a3c-b03b-7d74e588611d" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Speed of a Particle at a Given Time"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8cdced86-0585-5e4c-9f92-246be2506f2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186082365} {:answer/id #uuid "93dcf75c-ad61-5fd7-bb34-57eeaace8d4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186082366} {:answer/id #uuid "a6ab6971-aee2-5b5c-adbc-106e330fc3e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186082367} {:answer/id #uuid "ec6778bd-c7bf-5f13-9b7b-b9474fa23fa1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186082368} {:answer/id #uuid "26d6e280-700e-511c-b868-735d36246334" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186082369}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93dcf75c-ad61-5fd7-bb34-57eeaace8d4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186082366} :answer-field/id #uuid "db828abf-81f2-5446-8a9d-055dfcdb3a31" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186082364}] :question/id #uuid "6995c088-70db-5fcb-a926-3a5bb8ce6736" :question/math-academy-id "q-7151" :question/problem "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$r = ⟨\\frac{t^{2}}{2}, 3t + 7⟩, t > 0$.\nCalculate the speed of the particle at time $t = 4$."}]}
